      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): fold agent-menu help links into a Help submenu",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe sidebar footer agent menu lists every external help link (Docs, Get help, Discord community, View changelog) as a top-level row, so the menu is long and the primary actions (agent switching, Settings, Pair mobile device) drown in link rows.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nFolds the four external help links into a single \"Help\" flyout submenu, mirroring the existing session-menu flyout pattern (hover or click, `aria-haspopup`/`aria-expanded`, left-flip near the viewport edge). The agents list moves into its own scroll container so the menu root can stay overflow-visible for the flyout while long agent lists remain bounded.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe agent menu is shorter and cleaner: agent switching, \"What can X do?\", Settings, and Pair mobile device stay top-level; all help/community links sit one hover away under Help. No links were removed.\n\n## Evidence\n\nMock-gateway Control UI (dark, desktop):\n\n| Menu (compact) | Help flyout open |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![agent menu collapsed](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-106191/agent-menu-collapsed.png) | ![help flyout](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-106191/agent-menu-help-flyout.png) |\n\n- `ui/src/components/app-sidebar.test.ts` (Testbox, delegated): 42/42 passed, including the updated menu test asserting links no longer render top-level, the Help row exposes `aria-haspopup=\"menu\"`, and the open flyout renders the same four hrefs as before.\n- `agentChip.help` translated across all 20 locales via authenticated `ui:i18n:sync` (fallbacks=0).\n- Hosted CI on this head (see checks).\n",
        "branch": "claude/help-menu-compaction-89314c",
